    <comment>Tile caption.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Dashboard_GpuFan.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>مروحة GPU</value>
    <comment>Tile caption.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Dashboard_LoadDetail" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>الحمل {0} · {1}</value>
    <comment>Under a temperature: {0} = usage percentage (e.g. 45%), {1} = the chip's model name.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Dashboard_AsleepDetail" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>في وضع السكون · {0}</value>
    <comment>Under the GPU temperature while the graphics chip is powered down: {0} = its model name.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Dashboard_Cooling.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>التبريد</value>
    <comment>Card title.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Dashboard_CoolBoost.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>يتيح للوضع "تلقائي" تدوير المراوح بسرعة أكبر.</value>
    <comment>Describes CoolBoost (an Acer feature name shown above it). Auto = FanMode_Auto.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Dashboard_Performance.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>الأداء</value>
    <comment>Card title.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Dashboard_PowerPlan.Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>خطة طاقة Windows</value>
    <comment>Label above a list of Windows power plans.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Dashboard_PowerSource.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>مصدر الطاقة</value>
    <comment>Caption above 'Plugged in' or 'On battery'.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Dashboard_SystemTemperature.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>درجة حرارة النظام</value>
    <comment>Caption: the laptop's internal temperature.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Fans_Title.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>المراوح</value>
    <comment>Page title.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Fans_AutoBoost.Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>منع الاختناق الحراري</value>
    <comment>Name of an on/off setting in Auto mode: OpenSense adds fan speed as the chips heat up, so the processor does not throttle (slow itself down because it is too hot). Short.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Fans_AutoBoost.Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>يضيف سرعة فوق سرعة البرنامج الثابت مع ارتفاع حرارة الشرائح، ويصل إلى السرعة القصوى عند درجة الحرارة التي يبدأ عندها المعالج بخفض أدائه.</value>
    <comment>What the on/off setting does. "Throttle" = the processor slowing itself down because it is too hot.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Fans_CoolBoost.Description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>يرفع سرعات المراوح الخاصة بالبرنامج الثابت، التي يستخدمها الوضع "تلقائي" ويضيف إليها الوضع "مخصص".</value>
    <comment>Under the header "CoolBoost" (an Acer feature name). Auto, Custom = FanMode_Auto, FanMode_Custom.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Fans_BoostFixed.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>ثابتة</value>
    <comment>Segmented button per fan in Custom mode: add a fixed amount of speed (the slider below). Very short.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Fans_BoostCurve.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>منحنى</value>
    <comment>Segmented button per fan in Custom mode: the added speed follows a temperature curve. Very short.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Fans_Boost.Header" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>السرعة المضافة</value>
    <comment>Slider label: speed added on top of the firmware's, from 0% (firmware only) to 100% (full speed).</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Fans_Presets.Content" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>إعدادات مسبقة</value>
    <comment>Button that opens a list of ready-made fan curves.</comment>
  </data>
  <data name="Fans_PresetDefault.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>افتراضي</value>
    <comment>Fan curve preset name: the curve Auto uses when it speeds up the fans.</comment>
